      "text": "Ab initio calculation of the neutron-proton mass difference — 27 sections: Front matter; 1; Outline\n\n**Ab initio calculation of the neutron-proton mass difference**\n\n*Sz. Borsanyi1, S. Durr1,2, Z. Fodor1,2,3, C. Hoelbling1, S. D. Katz3,4, S. Krieg1,2, L. Lellouch5, T. Lippert1,2, A*\n\n57 pp, 27 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1; 1 Outline; 2 Lattice and action details; 2.1 Photon action; 2.2 The Dirac operator; 2.3 HEX smearing; 3 Analytical studies of various QED formulatio; 3.1 Computation of finite-volume corrections i; 3.2 Results for finite-volume corrections to t; 4 Finite-volume and lattice-spacing correction; 5 Finite-volume effects for composite particle; 5.1 Comparison to numerical QCD+QED results; 6 Algorithms; 6.1 Hybrid Monte Carlo; 6.2 Updating the photon field; 6.3 Cost issues; 7 Ensembles\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Proposition: Here, we provide a fully controlled ab initio calculation for these isospin splittings.\n- Proposition: Because the precision of the experimental result for the nucleon is far greater than ours, we additionally give the QED and QCD separation obtained using the experimental value of\n- Proposition: Supplementary Materials for Ab initio calculation of the neutron-proton mass difference Sz.\n- Proposition: However signiﬁcant complications were observed in simulations with a non-vanishing zero-mode (34).\n- Proposition: This setup is the one used in all previous studies which include QED corrections to hadronic observables in lattice QCD (7, 10, 11, 35).\n- Proposition: Finite-volume corrections in QEDTL on T4 The setup considered in this section, QEDTL on the four-torus T4 of dimensions L3 × T, is the one used in all previous studies which",
